  "body": "With several setups on screen, every origin triad looks alike - nothing in the viewport says whose zero is whose. Hover answers \"what is this\" only one gizmo at a time; the ask is to read it at a glance, and in a screenshot that goes onto a setup sheet.\n\n**Shape wanted:** every origin gizmo labels itself at its origin. Each work-offset triad draws the entity name the Setup pane already uses (`G54` for the first setup, `Setup2/WCS` for the second) just below its projected origin, in a bright label color at the ordinary overlay-label size; the dimmed neutral world axes draw `World` in the same dim gray as their lines. Names ride `gizmos()`: always visible, and an offset hidden by the Models-pane eye - or the world-axes toggle - loses its name with its lines, so no label clutter survives a hidden gizmo. Only the axis-tip `X`/`Y`/`Z` letters keep the big font.\n\n**Considered and dropped:** hover-only labels (not readable at a glance or screenshottable); per-tip offset glyphs (`G54 triad X` - six-plus glyphs per gizmo, clutter that buries the axes); coloring each offset's whole triad by setup (the axes' RGB channels already carry axis meaning).\n\n**Already built:** PR #645 implements exactly this, pinned by `gizmo_tests` (world axes labeled `World`, each triad labeled with its own offset name, name stands at the origin not the tips, hidden offsets drop their names). This issue exists so that PR has the right number to close: the review on #645 caught that it cited #641 - the unrelated lathe grooving bug - by mistake.\n",
